Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||08-15-2001||10:50 AM||||i just bought my 85 GT, the guy said it needed a new slave cylinder, but the mecanic yesterday said it needs a new clutch.  So i got screwed over there.  But i called the mecanic this morning and he said it may just be because its sitting for a little while, so pump the clutch and see if that works.  Ever since having the car i cannot get it into 3rd and forth EVER, and i cann't change gears when the car is on.  What is the problem here? The slave and master cylinder is fine.||||reg||9
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-15-2001||12:48 PM||||I am not clearly understanding you.Did you have your mech.install a new clutch?If so you need to bleed out the clutch hyd. system.To see if that helps you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||08-15-2001||01:04 PM||||Will it go into any gear while running?<BR>You mentioned that you couldn't get into 3rd or 4th ever meaning sitting still not running or running?<P>If it goes into 1st 2nd and reverse while running, adjust your selector cable!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Matthew_Fiero||08-15-2001||01:27 PM||||it does not go into 3rd or 4th eith way<BR>it goes into reverse 1st and 2nd with  car running and not running but not into reverse while running, if you attempt to do that then it makes a loud grinding sound.  The clutch is like 2 years old.  i do not need to press the clutch down if i want to go into first second or reverse<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-15-2001||01:37 PM||||Adjust your selector cable, that sounds like 90% cause of your problem.<BR>You MAY still have some small amount of air in the system.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TooManyFieros||08-15-2001||01:54 PM||||Sounds like a clutch hydraulic problem. Measure the travel at the clutch slave cylinder while someone depresses the clutch. You need 1.1"min. If you don't have it, go to V*archies websight and follow his Archism on bleeding the system. I really don't think you need a clutch at all.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Matthew_Fiero||08-15-2001||08:40 PM||||where is the selector cable?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||08-15-2001||09:46 PM||||Do you have a repair manual?<BR>If you don't, check the archives and do a search!<BR>BTW, the selector cable is on the transmission, have someone move your shifter from 1st to 2nd while you watch. The one that doesn't move is your selector cable. Since you can go from 1st to 2nd with the engine running, I don't feel like you have a clutch problem only a selector problem.||||reg||1
